  "reasoning": "Cook Political Report\u2019s statewide Partisan Voting Index lists Indiana as R+9, indicating the state voted about 9 points more Republican than the national average in recent presidential elections and currently has a Republican governor, a Republican-held Senate delegation, and a 7R-2D U.S. House split.[1][10] I could not locate any 2026-cycle head-to-head federal polling between named candidates within the last 45 days, and current-cycle coverage focuses mainly on state legislative candidate filing rather than competitive federal races, so the best available quantitative baseline for federal lean remains the R+9 PVI and Indiana\u2019s consistent recent history of electing Republicans statewide.[1][7][12] In the absence of fresh federal polling but with a structurally strong GOP advantage and no evidence of emerging competitiveness, I treat that approximate 9-point Republican edge as the effective current margin and rate the state as leaning Republican with relatively high confidence.[1][10]",
